# Admin Templates — Single Source of Truth

## The One Rule

There is **exactly one copy** of each admin template. The stub files have been deleted.

**AUTHORITATIVE files (the ONLY copies):**
- `dose/templates/admin/base_site.html`
- `dose/templates/admin/includes/custom_sidebar.html`

There is no `templates/admin/base_site.html`. It has been deleted. Do not recreate it.

## Valid Jazzmin Blocks

Only these blocks exist in Jazzmin's `admin/base.html` and will actually render:

| Block | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `extrahead` | CSS/meta in `<head>` |
| `sidebar` | Replace AdminLTE default sidebar |
| `page_content` | Main content area (includes breadcrumbs, content) |
| `extrajs` | Scripts + modal HTML at end of `<body>` |
| `extrastyle` | Extra styles in `<head>` |
| `title` | Page title |
| `footer` | Footer area |

**`{% block nav-global %}` is NOT a Jazzmin block.** Content inside it is silently discarded.
Any block not in the table above is silently discarded by Django template inheritance.

## All Modals and JS Must Go in `{% block extrajs %}`

- Theme picker modal
- Font controls modal
- Any future popup/overlay
- Any page-level script that depends on the DOM being ready

## Before Any Edit

1. You are editing `dose/templates/admin/base_site.html` — the ONLY copy
2. Get explicit approval from Michael or Shela before making any change
3. After any change: restart server + hard refresh + incognito test
4. Commit immediately with a clear message

## Do Not

- Add blocks that are not in the valid Jazzmin block table above
- Put modal HTML or scripts between block tags (they get discarded)
- Create new copies of these files anywhere else in the project
